  "conclusion": "The first visual preedit is synchronously cleared by the Text/Caret updates caused by provisional selected-range deletion. Pending input ownership survives, so the app keeps the confirmed document and history intact while the visible clause is absent.",
  "evidenceLimits": [
    "The exact native before/failure states and failing wait are recorded. Individual synthetic CompositionEvent dispatches are not separate trace records; their order and payload come from the frozen source, while pending composition and provisional deletion show the native update path ran.",
    "The browser input bridge is a single-line DOM input, but compositionupdate forwards its event data and ignores the following composing input event. Its newline-free surrounding DOM value is not evidence that this preedit payload was filtered.",
    "Six preceding paragraph check groups completed, including full multiline clipboard insertion and native undo/redo; the final composition group failed before cancellation/commit checks."
  ],
  "recommendedCorrection": [
    "Delete the provisional selection after establishing confirmed/pending ownership but before publishing the first nonempty visible clause. Guard against reentrant detach, new parent/presenter, changed host text or newer composition ownership.",
    "Keep presenter clearing for actual external Text/caret changes and preserve cancellation restoration, confirmed range mapping, native undo/redo and one document-session history entry.",
    "Add a native first-update regression with one selected Unicode paragraph and a multiline clause; require exact first preedit, paragraph/run styles and line indents before any second update.",
    "Keep the frozen browser one-update expectation unchanged; a duplicate compositionupdate would conceal the native defect."
  ]
